From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wifi: the radio kept on at the end of the post-beacon window
 in local wireless play

SetIRQ13's automatic power-down (W_POWER_TX bit1 clear) at the end of the post-beacon window:
- melonDS 1.1 turned the radio off in every mode but 3. A Mario Kart DS parent (mode 1, auto sleep on) then slept
  after each beacon, so over LAN its children's auth/association frames rarely landed while it was awake.
- 906e9eb (#2681) turns it off only in mode 0, which keeps a Mario Kart DS child (mode 2, W_POWER_TX=1) awake
  when it has to sleep to follow its parent: it could never join a group.
Now: never in manual mode (3), never for an MP parent sending beacons (IsMP && !IsMPClient), never in mode 2 with
the auto wake-up off (dswifi, #2680/#2681); associated with melonAP (Nintendo WFC) 906e9eb's rule (mode 0 only);
otherwise melonDS 1.1's rule, which a joining child needs. Adds "[diag]" traces (Debug level, rate-limited) of
IRQ13's decisions, the frames sent and received, and the MP state.
---
 src/Wifi.cpp | 260 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 234 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

